## 3. Deployment Steps

### 3.1 Build installers

```powershell
npm run tauri build
```

Produces, under `src-tauri/target/release/bundle/`:

- `nsis/Portal_0.1.0_x64-setup.exe` — user-level NSIS installer.
- `msi/Portal_0.1.0_x64_en-US.msi` — MSI package.

Both bundle the compiled `Portal.exe` with the embedded icon and frontend
assets.

### 3.2 Ship / install

1. Run the NSIS or MSI installer on a target Windows 10/11 x64 machine (no
   admin required for the NSIS user install).
2. Launch Portal — the tray icon appears; the widget window opens centered.
3. Toggle **Start at Login** (window footer checkbox or tray menu) — Portal
   writes its quoted exe path to `HKCU\...\CurrentVersion\Run`, so it starts
   with the user session on every login.
4. Close (✕) or Alt+F4 merely hides the window to tray; **Quit Portal** from
   the tray menu ends the app.

### 3.3 Distribution notes

- The installers are self-contained: WebView2 (the only system dependency) is
  preinstalled on Windows 10/11 and the Tauri bundler bootstraps a download
  otherwise.
- Machines without an Android SDK see a readable notice in the Android tab;
  everything else keeps working.
- Portal needs no firewall prompts (it only reads system tables and spawns
  local processes); servers it relaunches bind their own ports as before.

