## 4. Usage

- **Dev Servers tab** — every listening TCP port with its project name,
  framework badge (brand color), port and PID. Two filter toggles (top right):
  a **System** eye toggle hides/shows system-noise rows (svchost, lsass,
  System-bound ports, …), and a **Servers only** toggle shows just the
  dev-server rows (Next.js, React, Vite, Express, FastAPI, Streamlit, MLflow,
  Node, Python) — while it is active the System toggle is dimmed as
  not-applicable. Both choices persist between sessions and the hidden count
  is shown on the System toggle. One-click:
  🌐 opens `http://localhost:PORT` in the default browser; ↻ walks the process
  tree, kills it and relaunches the captured command line in the captured
  working directory.
- **Android tab** — detected SDK path (or a setup hint), each AVD with its
  live status badge, and ▶ boot / ⚡ cold boot / ■ stop actions.
- **Tray** — left-click toggles the window; right-click menu offers Show/Hide,
  Start at Login, and Quit. The tooltip shows the current listening-port count.
- The window footer mirrors live state: Start-at-Login toggle and the last
  snapshot time; snapshots refresh every 4 s.
